<title>USA: Virginia jobless rate dips to 4 percent for August.</title>
<headline>Virginia jobless rate dips to 4 percent for August.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Virginia's unemployment rate dipped to 4 percent in August from 4.5 percent in July and 4.6 percent a year ago, the Virginia Employment Commission said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The rate was the lowest for August in seven years and was well below the national average of 5.1 percent for August.</p>
<p>The city of Fairfax had the lowest unemployment rate for August, 1.4 percent, while Dickenson County had the highest, 20.3 percent.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
